  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">World Fisheries University Pilot Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to provide the FAO Conference with sufficient information to ascertain if a World Fisheries University under the auspices of FAO could feasibly add value to existing capacities for academic education in Fisheries Science with a view to enhancing fishery governance at all levels. The proposed World Fisheries University Pilot Program should lead to the following two outcomes:
1. 45 WFU laureates with internationally recognized Master?s degree in Fisheries Science from WFU;
2. Results from pilot used for FAO Conference decision in July 2019 concerning the Korean proposal for the establishment of a World Fisheries University</narrative>
  </description>
